Phase 3.1 — incremental Merkle repository index wired into the run plane
========================================================================
Node: IMP-EV-0004 (Incremental Merkle repository indexing)
Requirement: REQ-EV-0004 (ADAPT, owner subsystem context-engine, owner
label "Repository Index"); qualification gate QUAL-EV-0004
Phase context: Future-tasks Phase 3 item 1
Revision: commit 9bfc91a ("Phase 3.1 (IMP-EV-0004): incremental Merkle
repository index wired into the run plane") on main
Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC

WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: IMPLEMENTING-PARTIAL — logic-only,
modbit-retrieval NOT in the modbit-core dependency closure; the Merkle
incremental path had a latent root-drift defect and zero production
callers)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- crates/retrieval/src/walker.rs (new): read-only worktree walk via the
  `ignore` crate (v0.4.33, default features) — gitignore respect
  (global/per-repo/per-dir/excludes, nested + negation, require_git off
  so the policy is location-independent), hidden entries skipped,
  symlinks never followed, committed generated/vendor dirs policy-tagged
  and pruned (target/, node_modules/, dist/, vendor*) per docs/18,
  binary sniff (NUL in first 8 KiB), 256 KiB per-file cap (matches the
  search tool bound). WalkStats makes every skip class countable.
- crates/retrieval/src/task_index.rs (new): TaskIndex = MerkleIndex +
  RepositoryIndex + indexed_workspace_revision. build_at() walks the
  real worktree; apply_delta() folds IndexChange batches (latest state
  per path wins) incrementally, re-reading only changed paths from the
  worktree, evicting paths that are gone/unreadable/no-longer-indexable,
  and returning the only-affected-segments Recomputed evidence.
- crates/retrieval/src/merkle.rs (fix): apply_changes now PRUNES
  directories emptied by deletions (deepest-first, with evidence) —
  previously a stale empty-dir digest made the incremental root drift
  from a full rebuild. The existing unit test never caught it because it
  never compared roots after a dir-emptying deletion; it does now.
- crates/domain: IndexUpdated run-aggregate event (reason,
  workspace_revision, file_count, root_digest, recomputed[], bounded at
  128 entries with recomputed_truncated). docs/30 § Workspace/execution
  row added (additive).
- crates/core-runtime: TaskIndexWriter rides the run plane (store +
  session + RunPlaneShared + Mutex<TaskIndex>). Built ONCE at task start
  over the worktree; the build evidence is queued (RunPlaneShared
  pending queue) and drained onto the run aggregate immediately after
  RunStarted, preserving order. refresh_from_journal() drains the
  workspace change journal (the canonical FS delta source) for events
  after the indexed revision — wired at (a) change.apply, right after
  the journaled write, reason "change_apply"; (b) the turn boundary via
  the run observer, reason "turn_boundary" (a no-op when the journal has
  nothing new). A journal with no fresh events emits nothing.
- Closure: modbit-retrieval is now a path dependency of modbit-core-runtime
  (16 of 26 modbit-* crates in the product binary closure; was 15) —
  this resolves the module-outside-closure ground for the 2026-09-05
  premature-COMPLETE reset.
- Known boundary (documented, deferred by design): shell-spawned writes
  (shell.run producing files directly) carry no change-journal events,
  so they are not folded in by this wiring; the M3.2 query tool will
  reconcile the walk delta before serving any indexed answer (docs/18
  freshness rule: changed files covered by exact overlay or escalated).

